Companion (bottom-screen barter) — per-item weight on COMPANION_BARTER_ITEM.

The barter export carried `value` but no per-item weight, so the DS barter overlay could
only offer Default/Value sorting while the inventory and looting screens offer
Default/Weight/Value (BARTER_SORTS in CompanionScreen.kt existed solely to express that
gap). Player-side weights could in principle have been joined from the player's inventory,
but VENDOR items exist nowhere else on the Kotlin side — so the field has to come from here.

Emits the per-unit record weight (`Class::getWeight`, the same value the vanilla tooltip and
the encumbrance calculation use), mirroring the Lua `itemJson` "weight" field already on
COMPANION_INVENTORY_ITEM / COMPANION_CONTAINER_ITEM so all four item contexts carry the same
shape. Every barter item comes out of a container store, so its class always overrides
getWeight (the base Class::getWeight throw is unreachable here).

Authored as a DELTA against the already-patched tradewindow.cpp: that file is touched by
companion-barter-export.patch, companion-ui-sounds.patch and companion-barter-instance-id.patch,
so this is applied LAST in the chain rather than folded into the export patch — editing the
export patch's emit block would have broken the later patches' context lines.

diff --git a/apps/openmw/mwgui/tradewindow.cpp b/apps/openmw/mwgui/tradewindow.cpp
--- a/apps/openmw/mwgui/tradewindow.cpp
+++ b/apps/openmw/mwgui/tradewindow.cpp
@@ -890,6 +890,10 @@
                 << ",\"name\":\"" << companionJsonEscape(name) << "\""
                 << ",\"count\":" << stackCount
                 << ",\"value\":" << unitValue
+                // Companion: per-unit record weight, mirroring the Lua itemJson "weight" field on
+                // COMPANION_INVENTORY_ITEM / COMPANION_CONTAINER_ITEM, so the DS barter overlay can
+                // offer the same Weight sort as the inventory and looting screens.
+                << ",\"weight\":" << base.getClass().getWeight(base)
                 << ",\"cat\":\"" << companionBarterCategory(base) << "\""
                 << ",\"icon\":\"" << companionJsonEscape(icon) << "\""
                 << ",\"sellable\":" << (sellable ? "true" : "false")
